<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <!--
      Debug-only overlay.

      FOREGROUND_SERVICE_DATA_SYNC is used by exactly one thing: the bank-sync
      foreground service (LinkSyncForegroundService / background_sync.dart).
      The published release has no subscription yet, so nothing there can ever
      start a sync, and a permission the shipped app cannot exercise is one
      more line to justify on the Play data-safety form for no benefit.

      Declaring it here keeps a local build with keys.pro.json fully functional
      for daily use while the release manifest stays minimal. Move it into
      src/main/AndroidManifest.xml in the same update that turns Pro on for
      real: adding a normal (non-dangerous) permission in an update needs no
      user prompt and no re-acceptance.

      Note for editors: XML comments cannot contain a double hyphen, which is
      why flags are named in prose here rather than written out.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_DATA_SYNC" />
</manifest>
